{"name":"Dragon Dance","hex":"#9c3418","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dragon dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon dance is a form of traditional dance and performance in Chinese culture. Like the lion dance, it is most often seen during festive celebrations. The dance is performed by a team of experienced dancers who manipulate a long flexible giant puppet of a dragon using poles positioned at regular intervals along the length of the dragon. The dance team simulates the imagined movements of this mythological creature in a sinuous, undulating manner."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Chinese_draak.jpg/330px-Chinese_draak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_dance","wikidata":"Q636304"},{"title":"Dragon Dance (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Dragon Dance is a 2000 action game for the Game Boy Color developed by Natsume Co., Ltd. and published in the United States by Crave Entertainment. The game is a paddle-and-ball game similar to the arcade video game Breakout."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Dragon_Dance_GBC.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Dance_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q115137359"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon","wikidata":"Q7559"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b1/Dragon_Dance_Han_Dynasty_stone_relief.jpg/330px-Dragon_Dance_Han_Dynasty_stone_relief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thum